# SEO Rules (14 Rules)

## 22. Shared SEO Components
Build SEO, Schema, GTM components ONCE in shared starter. Use src/components/common/Metadata.astro and JsonLd.astro.

## 23. GTM Placement
GTM in base layout ONLY. GSC verified by DNS TXT record. Sitemap submitted after launch.

## 24. Unique Meta
Every page MUST have unique title (50-60 chars), unique description (120-160 chars), correct canonical URL.

## 25. Fallback Strategy
Pick ONE approach for defaults: Either site.ts OR Sanity siteSettings, NOT both.

## 26. robots.txt
Generated in code (src/pages/robots.txt.ts). Staging sites get noindex automatically.

## 27. Sitemap Auto-Discovery
NEVER hand-edit. Use import.meta.glob for static pages + Sanity queries for dynamic content.

## 28. SSR Sitemap with lastmod
Query Sanity with _updatedAt for lastmod dates. Production URLs only.

## 29. Default Schema Types
JSON-LD for: Organization, WebSite, WebPage, Breadcrumb, BlogPosting, Service, LocalBusiness, FAQPage.

## 30. Schema Override
Sanity SEO object includes schemaOverride field for custom JSON-LD per page.

## 31. SEO Panel in Sanity
Every document needs SEO object: title, description, canonical, noIndex, ogImage.

## 32. Site Settings Schema
Sanity siteSettings contains business info for LocalBusiness schema.

## 33. Open Graph
Every page needs og:title, og:description, og:image (1200x630), og:url, twitter:card.

## 34. Alt Text Required
imageWithAlt schema requires alt text. Validation blocks publish if missing.

## 35. Heading Structure
ONE h1 per page. H2, H3 in order (no skipping levels).
